      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas it a typo? These are some common possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 to 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting or maintenance range.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
